DESCRIPTION:From the folks who brought you the Renegade Orchestra\, Death 
 and Taxes Swing Band\, and the San Francisco Yiddish Combo...\n\nNot Loud 
 Concerts Presents…\n\nFantasy Waltz Night at the historic Chapel of the 
 Flowers in Berkley\, April 25 From 7:00-8:30\n\nTake your carriage (or Bar
 t) to a magical\, historical dance space located in Berkeley for a night o
 f waltzes presented by a live chamber orchestra.\n\nThe evening begins at 
 7:00 with a short beginning waltz lesson presented by dance master Colin W
 illiams\, followed by the orchestra picking up their bows to present a sel
 ection of danceable waltzes. From the Viennese waltzes of Johann Strauss I
 I\, to the magical sounds of Disney\, to the rollicking waltzes of the fro
 ntier\, members of the Renegade Orchestra will get your feet moving in 3/4
  time.\n\nCome in your ball gowns\, fantasy attire or in casual garb\, beg
 inners and seasoned dancers are all welcome. The floor is wood\, the space
  is magical and the music is of course\, not too loud. Complimentary coffe
 e and cookies will be available.\n\nLocated at 3049 Adeline St\, very clos
 e to the Ashby Bart station and with a private parking lot as well as stre
 et parking. 18 and up\, children will not be admitted.\n\n3049 Adeline St.
  (this venue is new and may not appear on maps. Don’t go to Chapel of th
 e Chimes\, that is a funeral home.)
LOCATION:Chapel of the Flowers\, 3049 Adeline Street\, Berkeley\, CA 94703
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
